<title>JAPAN: Russia to resume platinum exports - Japan traders.</title>
<headline>Russia to resume platinum exports - Japan traders.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's platinum group metal (PGM) export agency Almazjuvelirexport informed Japanese buyers that it would resume platinum exports next week, local traders said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The Russian agency recently resumed its palladium exports to Japan, but platinum shipments had been delayed.</p>
<p>&quot;Almaz told us that platinum shipments were being delayed because of problems involved in packaging platinum. But they informed us they will be able to resume shipments next week,&quot; said a trader at a major Japanese trade house.</p>
<p>The six-month suspension of Russian PGM exports, caused by bureaucratic problems there, sent world palladium and platinum prices soaring and caused an acute supply tightness.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
